2. Once the array is sorted, the second largest integer is the second element in the sorted array. After sorting, the largest integer will be the last element in the array, and the second largest will be right before it. Thus, the second element from the end of the sorted array represents the second largest integer in the original array.

Here is a Python program that implements this algorithm. This program sorts the array and then retrieves the second element, which is the second largest integer:

